---
import PiDriveTransfer from "../../layouts/PiDriveTransfer.astro";
---

<PiDriveTransfer
  title="Pi Drive Transfer - In-Between Labs"
  description="Matt Blethen's personal Google Drive backup and download utility, using rclone on his own Raspberry Pi with read-only Drive access."
  canonical="https://inbetweenlabs.com/pi-drive-transfer"
>
  <section aria-labelledby="tool-title" class="card glow p-6 sm:p-8 md:p-12">
    <p class="inline-flex rounded-full border border-white/10 bg-white/5 px-3 py-1 text-xs text-white/70">
      Personal utility · Single-user use
    </p>
    <h1 id="tool-title" class="mt-5 text-4xl sm:text-5xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Pi Drive Transfer</h1>
    <p class="mt-4 text-lg text-white/80 leading-relaxed">
      Personal Google Drive downloads, on Matt's own storage.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-4 text-white/70 leading-relaxed">
      Pi Drive Transfer is Matt Blethen's personal file backup and download utility. It uses the third-party,
      open-source <a href="https://rclone.org/" class="underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-white">rclone</a>
      tool on his own Raspberry Pi to connect directly to the Google Drive API and download selected personal
      files onto storage he owns.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-4 text-white/70 leading-relaxed">
      Matt owns and operates the Google OAuth client named Pi Drive Transfer. The utility is for his own use;
      it is not offered as a public backup service. This website provides information about the utility and
      does not connect visitors' Google Drive accounts.
    </p>
    <div class="mt-7 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
      <a href="/pi-drive-transfer/privacy" class="btn-primary">Read the privacy notice</a>
      <a href="mailto:inbetweenlabs@gmail.com" class="btn-ghost">Contact Matt</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="access-title" class="mt-6 card p-6 sm:p-8">
    <h2 id="access-title" class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight">How Google Drive access works</h2>
    <div class="mt-4 space-y-4 text-white/70 leading-relaxed">
      <p>
        Google authorization is handled through rclone. The requested permission is
        <code class="break-all text-white/90">https://www.googleapis.com/auth/drive.readonly</code>.
        It allows reading and downloading Drive file contents and metadata across the connected account's
        Drive, even though Matt chooses which files to download. It does not permit uploading, changing,
        or deleting Drive files.
      </p>
      <p>
        OAuth tokens are stored in the local rclone configuration for ongoing access. Downloaded files stay
        on Matt's own storage until he deletes them. No Drive files or OAuth credentials are collected by
        this public website, and no custom application server receives visitors' Drive data.
      </p>
      <p>
        Drive data is used only for this personal download and backup workflow. It is not sold, used for
        advertising, or used to train AI models. Google Drive desktop uploads on Matt's separate computer
        use the official Google Drive app and are outside Pi Drive Transfer.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="control-title" class="mt-6 card p-6 sm:p-8">
    <h2 id="control-title" class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Control and contact</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 text-white/70 leading-relaxed">
      Access can be removed through
      <a href="https://myaccount.google.com/connections" class="underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-white">Google Account connections</a>.
      Removing access stops future authorized transfers; existing local copies must be deleted separately.
      The <a href="/pi-drive-transfer/privacy" class="underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-white">privacy notice</a>
      explains access, storage, retention, and deletion in more detail.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-4 text-white/70 leading-relaxed">
      Owner and developer: Matt Blethen / In-Between Labs.<br />
      Questions: <a href="mailto:inbetweenlabs@gmail.com" class="break-all underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-white">inbetweenlabs@gmail.com</a>.
    </p>
  </section>
</PiDriveTransfer>
